{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":23,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.exact_order_of_conjecture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.exact_order_of_conjecture","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorOrderLawGeneral.lean#L242-L250","doc":"**(CONDITIONAL on the conjecture.)**  If the exact-order conjecture holds for a\ndeficit family `D`, then at every order `A ≥ 2` the order is **exactly** `2(A−1)`\n(the lower bound is achieved).  Fully verified modulo the single open class instance\n`MilnorExactOrderConjecture D` (§3b-cond conditional result). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.MilnorExactOrderConjecture.tight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.MilnorExactOrderConjecture.tight","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorOrderLawGeneral.lean#L239-L239","doc":"At every order `A ≥ 2` the deficit factors as `h^{2(A−1)}` times a cofactor\nwith nonzero leading value — the lower bound is tight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.MilnorExactOrderConjecture.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.MilnorExactOrderConjecture.mk","kind":"ctor","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorOrderLawGeneral.lean#L236-L236","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.MilnorExactOrderConjecture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.MilnorExactOrderConjecture","kind":"class","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorOrderLawGeneral.lean#L224-L240","doc":"**(CONJECTURE, primary — OPEN.)**  The exact Milnor order law for the actual\nBrunnian trace-deficit family `D : ℕ → ℝ → ℝ` (`D A h = 1 − τ_A(h)`): at **every**\norder `A ≥ 2` the proved lower bound `order(D_A) ≥ 2(A−1)` is **TIGHT**, i.e. there\nis a cofactor with `D_A h = h^{2(A−1)}·cofactor h` whose value at `h = 0` (the\nleading coefficient) is **nonzero**.  Equivalent to the length-`A` Milnor\nμ̄-invariant of the `A`-component Brunnian link being nonzero.\n\nThis carrier has **NO instance** — the honest open state — confirmed only at A=3\n(PROVED, `borromean_tight_slice`) and A=4 (MEASURED, #4378).  The field is\ncontent-bearing (a parameter-quantified equality in the shape of the claim), not an\nempty marker; fabricating an instance would launder two points into a universal\nlaw. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.tauL4MeasuredOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.tauL4MeasuredOrder","kind":"def","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorOrderLawGeneral.lean#L217-L220","doc":"Measured A=4 leading Milnor order (#4378): `n ≈ 6.06`, consistent with\n`leadingOrder 4 = 6 = 2(4−1)`.  MEASURED, not proved — recorded; no theorem asserts\n`= 6`, matching the anti-laundering discipline. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.tauL4Measured_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.tauL4Measured_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorOrderLawGeneral.lean#L215-L215","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.tauL4Measured","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.tauL4Measured","kind":"def","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorOrderLawGeneral.lean#L209-L213","doc":"Measured genuine-Brunnian level trace at the substrate for A=4 (#4378, cited to\n`a4-h12-brunnian-deficit-measure.witness.json`, `w₄ = [[A₀₁,A₁₂],A₂₃]`,\nBrunnian-verified via the strand-forgetting map): `τ_L₄ ≈ 1.000146 > 1`.  MEASURED\ninput — NOT a proved closed form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.borromean_tight_slice","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.borromean_tight_slice","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorOrderLawGeneral.lean#L197-L205","doc":"**A=3 exact-order slice, PROVED.**  The A=3 slice of the general exact-order\nconjecture (§5) holds: a nonzero leading coefficient `r = 3/4` and a cofactor with\n`D_3 h = h^{2(3−1)} · cofactor h`, `cofactor 0 = r ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.borromean_cofactor_ne_zero_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.borromean_cofactor_ne_zero_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorOrderLawGeneral.lean#L192-L195","doc":"The A=3 cofactor is nonzero at `h = 0` (`= 3/4`): the order is **exactly** 4,\nnot an accidental higher vanishing — the lower bound `2(3−1)=4` is TIGHT. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.borromean_deficit_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.borromean_deficit_factor","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorOrderLawGeneral.lean#L182-L190","doc":"Trace-deficit closed form: `1 − τ_Borr = h^{leadingOrder 3} · (3 + h²)/(h²+4)`\n`= h⁴ · (3 + h²)/(h²+4)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.tauBorromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.tauBorromean","kind":"def","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorOrderLawGeneral.lean#L178-L180","doc":"The Borromean `H₃` Markov-trace closed form (restated from #4360):\n`τ_Borr(h) = (4 + h² − 3h⁴ − h⁶)/(h²+4)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.brunnian_deficit_order_lower_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.brunnian_deficit_order_lower_bound","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorOrderLawGeneral.lean#L160-L169","doc":"**★ HEADLINE — the all-A order lower bound.**  For a Markov trace `τ` and a\nlength-`A` Brunnian iterated commutator (`A = n+2 ≥ 2`) built from h-order-2 levels,\nthe trace deficit `τ(w_A)` is divisible by `h^{leadingOrder A} = h^{2(A−1)}`:\n`order(D_A) ≥ 2(A−1)` for **every** `A`.  Proved from the h-adic filtration; 0\nfree parameters.  (The physical deficit is `1 − τ_A = −τ(w_A)` under the Brunnian\nnormalisation `τ_A(0) = 1`; the divisibility is sign-independent.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.iterCommTower_leadingOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.iterCommTower_leadingOrder","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorOrderLawGeneral.lean#L152-L158","doc":"Restated against `leadingOrder`: the length-`A` tower (`A = n+2`) has h-order\n`leadingOrder A = 2(A−1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.iterCommTower_hasOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.iterCommTower_hasOrder","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorOrderLawGeneral.lean#L139-L150","doc":"**Order induction.**  If every level `c i` has h-order 2 (one h² factor), the\nlength-`(n+2)` tower has h-order `2(n+1) = 2((n+2)−1)`.  Pure induction on `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.iterCommTower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.iterCommTower","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorOrderLawGeneral.lean#L131-L137","doc":"**Left-normed iterated commutator tower.**  `iterCommTower c n` models the\nlength-`(n+2)` Brunnian iterated commutator `w_{n+2} = [c_{n+1}, [c_n, [… , c_0]]]`\nof pure-braid band generators (`c i` = the h-order-2 commutator building block at\nlevel `i`).  `V 0 = c 0`; `V (n+1) = [c (n+1), V n] = c(n+1)·V n − V n·c(n+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.HasOrder.trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.HasOrder.trace","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorOrderLawGeneral.lean#L115-L121","doc":"**Trace transfer.** Any R-linear functional (the Markov trace is one) maps an\nh-order-`k` element to a scalar divisible by `h^k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.HasOrder.commutator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.HasOrder.commutator","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorOrderLawGeneral.lean#L102-L113","doc":"**Commutators add h-orders** — the h²-per-level engine of the order law.\n`[x, y] = x·y − y·x` has order `p + q` when `x, y` have orders `p, q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.HasOrder.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.HasOrder.mul","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorOrderLawGeneral.lean#L93-L100","doc":"**Products add h-orders.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.HasOrder.of_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.HasOrder.of_le","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorOrderLawGeneral.lean#L86-L91","doc":"Downward monotone: order ≥ `k'` implies order ≥ `k` for `k ≤ k'`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.HasOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.HasOrder","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorOrderLawGeneral.lean#L82-L84","doc":"`x : A` has h-adic order ≥ `k`: it is `h^k` times something, `h` central. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.leadingOrder_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.leadingOrder_four","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorOrderLawGeneral.lean#L70-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.leadingOrder_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.leadingOrder_three","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorOrderLawGeneral.lean#L69-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.leadingOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.leadingOrder","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorOrderLawGeneral.lean#L66-L67","doc":"Leading Milnor order of the `A`-component Brunnian trace deficit, `2(A−1)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}